      {
        "id": "intro",
        "type": "nodetool.workflows.base_node.Comment",
        "data": {
          "comment": "# Sci-fi Game Model Starter Pack\n\nReusable sci-fi GLB models: a scout robot with an idle animation, a drone, cargo, crystals and modular station pieces. Use them to block out or dress a 3D game level without generating assets first.\n\n**How it works:** Fourteen Model3D constant nodes, from \"Scout robot\" to \"Beacon\", each load one shipped GLB and connect to a matching output such as \"Scout robot output\". Running exposes every model as a named output. Models use meters, Y up, forward -Z and ground-level origins, and station pieces sit on a 2 m grid. They are visuals only, so add gameplay colliders separately and keep the model on a visual child of the physics root. The robot has an Idle clip, with no skeleton or locomotion clips. It runs locally with no model or key.\n\n**Try this:** Run it, download \"Floor tile output\" from its preview, upload it to your project, and import it into a 3D game next to \"Wall panel output\" to check the 2 m grid lines up."
        },
